---
description: Arcane edit markers and sync-conflict avoidance
globs: **/*.cs,**/*.yml,**/*.yaml,**/*.ftl,**/*.xaml,**/*.toml,**/*.json,**/*.py
alwaysApply: true
---
Canonical text: `.agents/rules/arcane-edit-markers.md`, `.agents/rules/fork-trajectory-priority.md`, `.agents/rules/merge-conflict-resolution.md`. This adapter exists because those files are not auto-loaded.

Our own changes carry Arcane markers only:

- one added line: trailing `Arcane`, never `Arcane-Start`
- two or more added lines: `// Arcane-Start` / `// Arcane-End`, `# Arcane-Start` / `# Arcane-End`
- one changed line: trailing `// Arcane-Edit: <old> > <new>` or `# Arcane-Edit: <old> > <new>`
- two or more changed lines: `// Arcane-Edit-Start` / `// Arcane-Edit-End`, `# Arcane-Edit-Start` / `# Arcane-Edit-End`
- over 5 changed lines: comment the payload inside an `Arcane-Edit-Start` / `Arcane-Edit-End` block
- merge adjacent Arcane blocks of the same kind into one pair; never merge an `Arcane-Start` block into an `Arcane-Edit-Start` block
- a block and a lone line beside it do not combine: the block covers two or more lines, the lone line was never a block
- added `using` goes after all others, as a trailing `Arcane` or inside a block
- never put a bare `-Start` or `-End` on a line instead of a pair

Never write `Trauma - `, `<Trauma>`, `Goobstation-`, `/* Trauma`, or any other fork's marker on our own change.

No marker inside Arcane owner-local paths: `Modules/Arcane/**`, `Content.Arcane.*`, `Resources/_Arcane/**`. Nothing syncs there, so a marker is noise.

Mark Arcane changes inside `Content.Trauma.*`, `Resources/_Trauma/**`, `*.Trauma.cs`, `Content.Medical.*`, `Resources/_Shitmed/**`, and vanilla root paths. Those paths are owner-local for us but upstream surface for a sync, so an unmarked change there is indistinguishable from a Trauma change and gets reverted.

Changing a line that carries an upstream marker makes it ours:

```yaml
cost: 3000 # Trauma - was 1800, its useless for mining
cost: 6000 # Arcane-Edit: 1800 > 3000
```

Leave upstream markers on lines we did not touch alone, and never convert them in bulk as a side effect of unrelated work.

When a sync conflict must be resolved, the resolved line takes the marker of whoever wrote it. Our resolution is ours, so it carries an Arcane marker. Read all three versions, merge semantically, and never blanket-resolve with `git checkout --ours/--theirs`, `-X ours`, or `-X theirs`.
